{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01P6SNmCSVMNb2tVvBQLraYc","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /work/.ard/61/triage-lead.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"38ba34d0-3424-47b2-95c9-944823ae2775","uuid":"4dbfe193-47c9-4b78-b7b6-a8d52d7f0b47","timestamp":"2026-11-23T16:43:12.293Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"create","filePath":"/work/.ard/61/triage-lead.md","content":"---\nrole: lead\nstatus: done\nattempt: 1\nnext: [triage:engineer]\nworker: engineer\n---\nAdds a monthly janitor that removes per-issue directories under .ard/ for issues closed more than 90 days ago, committing the deletion through the existing committer. The dependency the issue names appears to have landed already (the committer package exists and cites it), so the work can start now.\n\n## Routing\n- triage:engineer: implementation steps for the janitor loop, how it finds closed issues and their close dates, how it commits through the committer, and a test plan.\n- worker engineer: code change with unit tests.\n\n## Open issues\n- The repository has no architect, product-manager or documentation-planner triage roles. This change adds a new background loop and may touch serve's loop list and the proposal docs, so a maintainer may want to check the design during review.\n- The janitor deletes files from main. The engineer's plan should make sure it never touches the protected role and config directories under .ard/, or the per-issue directory of an issue that is still open or was reopened.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01P6SNmCSVMNb2tVvBQLraYc","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLCFhXrehDF9xGU4GhXj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I routed issue #61 as **done**. The engineer triage role writes the plan, and the engineer worker implements it. The result is in `.ard/61/triage-lead.md`.\n\n- **The request:** add a monthly job that deletes `.ard/<issue#>/` for issues closed more than 90 days ago, committing the deletion through the committer.\n- **Why it isn't blocked:** the issue says it depends on #17. That work looks like it has already landed. `internal/committer/committer.go:64` refers to a decision made on #17, and other code cites it too. I didn't check the state of #17 on GitHub.\n- **Why only the engineer triage role:** the only triage roles that exist are lead and engineer. No architect, product-manager or documentation-planner roles exist. The eng-review reviewer has no `when:` rule, so it runs on the pull request anyway.\n\nThe file also gives a maintainer two open points:\n- This change adds a new background loop and may touch serve's loop list and `docs/proposal.md`. There is no architect or documentation role to review that design during triage, so someone may want to check it when the pull request comes in.\n- The plan should make sure the job never deletes the protected role and config directories under `.ard/`. It should also skip the directory of any issue that is still open or was reopened."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":639,"cache_read_input_tokens":14450,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":639},"output_tokens":418,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"38ba34d0-3424-47b2-95c9-944823ae2775","uuid":"7ff111fa-fa64-440c-a110-b4a311897